# Integrations

Inventory: `docs/integrations-reference.md`. Optional keys must degrade (UI banner + empty/template), not take down the process.

## Two key planes

| Plane | Store | Who | Examples |
|---|---|---|---|
| Platform | `platform_api_keys` (encrypted, non-tenant) | InfoGenie-paid, admin-only | OpenAI, Anthropic, Gemini, Perplexity, DataForSEO, Firecrawl, Resend |
| User | `services/credentials/vault.js` AES-256-GCM per `(user_id, platform)` | Tenant’s own accounts | Semrush, Shopify, Google Ads OAuth tokens |

`hydrate()` overlays platform DB values onto `process.env` (DB wins). Then rebuild shared SDK clients. Blocklist platform keys from per-user Settings (`403`).

Production **refuses to boot** without `CREDENTIAL_ENCRYPTION_KEY`. Never log vault plaintext, refresh tokens, or webhook secrets.

## OAuth (keep callbacks stable)

| Flow | Callback |
|---|---|
| Google Ads | `/api/integrations/google-ads/oauth/callback` |
| Meta Ads | `/api/integrations/meta-ads/oauth/callback` |
| Google Workspace (Gmail+Drive+Calendar, vault key `google_workspace`) | `/api/integrations/workspace/oauth/callback` |
| Social login | Google / Facebook / Microsoft — buttons hide when env is missing |

Redirect URIs are `${PUBLIC_URL}<callback>`. Do not change paths casually; they are allow-listed at the provider.

## Wiring a new vendor

1. Server module under `services/<vendor>/` with a `test`/`status` probe.
2. Permission-matrix prefix.
3. Tenant-scoped persistence if you store results.
4. Timeouts, friendly error hints (401/scope/quota), and SSRF guards on inbound webhooks (see crisis-radar Slack pattern).
5. Admin live-test quirks live in `.agents/memory/platform-key-tests.md` (read-only): some vendors return 200 on a bad key.

Do not proxy arbitrary user URLs. Do not send user data to a new vendor without an existing product surface that already does so.
